msgctxt "#32040"
msgid "Auto detects the TV resolution and caps the quality accordingly (up to 4K on a 4K panel, up to 1080p on Full HD). Pick a fixed value to limit quality on weaker devices."
msgstr "Auto detects the TV resolution and caps the quality accordingly (up to 4K on a 4K panel, up to 1080p on Full HD). Pick a fixed value to limit quality on weaker devices."

msgctxt "#32041"
msgid "Off = no subtitles. Original = the subtitle track YouTube marks as default. Preferred language = the Content language track, auto-translated by YouTube when the uploader has no such track."
msgstr "Off = no subtitles. Original = the subtitle track YouTube marks as default. Preferred language = the Content language track, auto-translated by YouTube when the uploader has no such track."

msgctxt "#32042"
msgid "Leave empty to use the Content language. Example: ro for Romanian subtitles on an English video."
msgstr "Leave empty to use the Content language. Example: ro for Romanian subtitles on an English video."

msgctxt "#32043"
msgid "Country used for search, Trending, Live and Trailers results."
msgstr "Country used for search, Trending, Live and Trailers results."

msgctxt "#32044"
msgid "Two-letter country code not listed above, for example PL, KR, VN."
msgstr "Two-letter country code not listed above, for example PL, KR, VN."

msgctxt "#32045"
msgid "Language of the returned metadata and of the Trending/Live/Trailers category searches."
msgstr "Language of the returned metadata and of the Trending/Live/Trailers category searches."

msgctxt "#32046"
msgid "Language code not listed above, for example he, fa, uk, zh-TW, fil. Category searches fall back to English words for languages without a translation table."
msgstr "Language code not listed above, for example he, fa, uk, zh-TW, fil. Category searches fall back to English words for languages without a translation table."

msgctxt "#32047"
msgid "Category listed when Trending is opened without a choice."
msgstr "Category listed when Trending is opened without a choice."

msgctxt "#32048"
msgid "Category listed when Live is opened without a choice."
msgstr "Category listed when Live is opened without a choice."

msgctxt "#32049"
msgid "Original plays the original audio track only. Localized prefers an audio track in your Content language and falls back to the original when none exists."
msgstr "Original plays the original audio track only. Localized prefers an audio track in your Content language and falls back to the original when none exists."

msgctxt "#32050"
msgid "On: after a video ends the next one from the same list keeps playing, in the exact order you see (Trending, Random music, Live, Search results, a channel). A video started from outside this add-on (TMDb Movies) gets a random music track instead. Off: nothing plays on its own."
msgstr "On: after a video ends the next one from the same list keeps playing, in the exact order you see (Trending, Random music, Live, Search results, a channel). A video started from outside this add-on (TMDb Movies) gets a random music track instead. Off: nothing plays on its own."

msgctxt "#32051"
msgid "On: the clicked video still plays first, but what follows is shuffled instead of the list order. Same pool as Autoplay, just random."
msgstr "On: the clicked video still plays first, but what follows is shuffled instead of the list order. Same pool as Autoplay, just random."

msgctxt "#32052"
msgid "How many videos a list page shows. Larger pages build longer playlists."
msgstr "How many videos a list page shows. Larger pages build longer playlists."

msgctxt "#32053"
msgid "How many videos each subscribed channel contributes to the feed."
msgstr "How many videos each subscribed channel contributes to the feed."

msgctxt "#32054"
msgid "Writes detailed extraction and playback lines to kodi.log and bypasses the listing cache."
msgstr "Writes detailed extraction and playback lines to kodi.log and bypasses the listing cache."

msgctxt "#32055"
msgid "Deletes the downloaded listings, the music pool and the queue state."
msgstr "Deletes the downloaded listings, the music pool and the queue state."

